# s []N_GRID m draws numbers on a grid: each cell filled from the scale
# s (a Scale: []S_CALE 1 gray, 2 heat, 3 diverging, named in the Svg
# library) and its number written in it, in dark ink on a light fill
# and light ink on a dark one (QD8, ask G2).
== SOURCE
([]S_CALE 2) []N_GRID 1 2
== RESULT
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="48" height="24" viewBox="0 0 48 24" role="img">
<rect width="48" height="24" fill="#f8fafc"/>
<rect x="0" y="0" width="24" height="24" fill="#440154"/>
<text x="12" y="12" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#f8fafc" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">1</text>
<rect x="24" y="0" width="24" height="24" fill="#fde725"/>
<text x="36" y="12" font-family="monospace" font-size="11" fill="#1f2937" text-anchor="middle" dominant-baseline="central">2</text>
<path d="M0 0H48M0 24H48M0 0V24M24 0V24M48 0V24" stroke="#cbd5e1" stroke-width="1" fill="none"/>
</svg>
